Observability: SDD

Purpose:
  The .sdd system's observability, runtime diagnostics and incident
  engine component. Defines how production runtime will be monitored,
  log/metrics/trace policy, alerting rules, health check mechanism,
  and incident lifecycle. Project-specific runtime state is stored in
  .sdd/projects/{project_name}/observability/.

Owns: ./

Modes:
  MONITOR   — runtime monitoring and health check
  ALERT     — alerting and incident detection
  DIAGNOSE  — root cause analysis and diagnostics
  INCIDENT  — incident lifecycle management
  RECOVER   — recovery and rollback decision support

Rules:
  [OBS1]  Observability data MUST be treated as evidence, not assumption.
  [OBS2]  AI MUST correlate metrics, logs, and traces before diagnosing.
  [OBS3]  Alert severity MUST be project-contextual.
  [OBS4]  Incident MUST be distinguished from alert: alert = suspicion,
          incident = confirmed business/system impact.
  [OBS5]  Root cause analysis MUST include confidence level, not just
          likely cause.
  [OBS6]  Incident ? Task flow MUST be automatic for confirmed incidents.
  [OBS7]  Recurring failures MUST trigger ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW_REQUIRED.
  [OBS8]  Deploy correlation MUST be maintained: incident ? suspected
          deploy ? code change.
  [OBS9]  Sensitive data (password, token, session, card, secret, PII)
          MUST NOT appear in logs; violation = SECURITY_VIOLATION.
  [OBS10] Rollback decisions for production MUST respect project policy.
  [OBS11] AI decision provenance MUST be reproducible.
  [OBS12] System records decision summary, not full chain-of-thought.
  [OBS13] Observability data MUST be classified.
  [OBS14] Cost and token metrics are required for AI operations.
  [OBS15] Skill performance metrics drive improvement decisions.
  [OBS16] Event ordering is guaranteed per execution_id.
  [OBS17] Event consumers MUST be idempotent.
  [OBS18] Correlation ID links workflow; Causation ID links causal chain.
  [OBS19] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to observability output.
  [OBS20] Agent MUST NOT use emojis or decorative symbols in observability output.

Pillars:
  Logs: Structured logging with correlation IDs
  Metrics: Business and technical metrics
  Traces: Distributed tracing across services

ReadOrder:
   1  @logging.sdd
   2  @metrics.sdd
   3  @tracing.sdd
   4  @health.sdd
   5  @incident.sdd

Navigation:
  Observability: @observability/INDEX.sdd
  Logging: @observability/logging.sdd
  Metrics: @observability/metrics.sdd
  Tracing: @observability/tracing.sdd
  Health: @observability/health.sdd
  Incident: @observability/incident.sdd
  ProjectObservability: @projects/{project_name}/observability/INDEX.sdd

State: +